          "heading": "Benhard Janse van Rensburg stretchered off as Bristol defeat champions Northampton Saints",
          "body": "England centre Benhard Janse van Rensburg was stretchered off following a significant head injury during Saturday’s Premiership victory over Northampton Saints. The midfielder was knocked out after an awkward collision with Henry Pollock just before half-time, requiring an eight-minute stoppage for medical treatment at Ashton Gate. While Bristol secured a 41-26 win, the incident creates a midfield concern for Steve Borthwick. Elsewhere in the same match, Harry Randall impressed at scrum-half while Tommy Freeman struggled in an experimental full-back role."
