          "heading": "Hector Patterson attracts Bath interest amid potential England allegiance switch",
          "body": "Edinburgh scrum-half Hector Patterson is reportedly being monitored by Bath ahead of next season as leading clubs in England and France track the 21-year-old. Patterson, the son of former Scotland scrum-half Derrick Patterson, has represented Scotland through the age-grade ranks up to the U20s. However, because he remains uncapped at senior level, he is also eligible to represent England through a grandparent, leaving his international future open as Edinburgh face a fight to retain him beyond his current contract."
